# SENTINEL LAB ingress sensor (`suricata`): HTTP flood at the rate-limiter's client-facing port 8080. Slowloris, UDP
# flood and TCP exhaustion never pass the rate-limiter and are handled by the target taps (web-tap.rules,
# target-tap.rules). Thresholds come from defense/suricata/calibrate.py runs, not estimates:
#
#   GET requests from one source per 10 s (maximum over the busiest window, two runs each)
#     legitimate, default legit-load (10 users)  132-146
#     legitimate, busy (45 users, half the think time) 785-877
#     HTTP flood (attacker-http-flood)           1089-1159
#
# 400 is the geometric mean of the default legitimate load and the flood (2.7x either way). Legitimate load from ONE
# source above about 40 req/s cannot be told from the flood by rate, so it alerts (the busy profile does); that is the
# same limit the ML detector has. Counting requests, not packets: the previous packet-count rule (200 per 10 s) alerted
# on ordinary legitimate load.

alert http any any -> any 8080 (msg:"SENTINEL LAB: possible HTTP flood"; flow:established,to_server; http.method; content:"GET"; threshold:type both, track by_src, count 400, seconds 10; classtype:attempted-dos; sid:1000001; rev:3;)
